{"module":"enforcement","voice":"female","duration":172.6,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Immigration enforcement now","start":0.0,"end":1.94,"words":[[0.05,0.86],[0.86,1.58],[1.58,1.83]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Immigration enforcement increasingly runs through local police and 911-style reports.","start":2.74,"end":9.43,"words":[[2.8,3.55],[3.55,4.23],[4.23,4.99],[4.99,5.29],[5.29,5.51],[5.51,5.97],[5.97,6.34],[6.34,6.57],[6.57,8.38],[8.38,8.91]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This lesson covers how that works and what the evidence shows.","start":9.78,"end":13.21,"words":[[9.82,10.02],[10.02,10.35],[10.35,10.69],[10.69,10.89],[10.89,11.1],[11.1,11.37],[11.37,11.57],[11.57,11.77],[11.77,11.9],[11.9,12.38],[12.38,12.71]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The history is in “Borders.”","start":13.56,"end":15.51,"words":[[13.61,13.76],[13.76,14.27],[14.27,14.42],[14.42,14.57],[14.57,15.01]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Local police as immigration agents","start":15.86,"end":18.68,"words":[[15.91,16.43],[16.43,16.87],[16.87,17.04],[17.04,17.9],[17.9,18.6]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Section 287(g) of federal immigration law lets ICE deputize local police and sheriffs to carry out some immigration enforcement.","start":19.38,"end":29.33,"words":[[19.43,19.9],[19.9,21.66],[21.93,22.09],[22.09,22.63],[22.63,23.39],[23.39,23.55],[23.55,23.86],[23.86,24.09],[24.09,24.78],[24.78,25.24],[25.24,25.62],[25.62,25.86],[25.86,26.32],[26.32,26.47],[26.47,26.78],[26.78,27.01],[27.01,27.24],[27.24,28.01],[28.01,28.78]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The number of 287(g) agreements expanded sharply in 2025.","start":29.68,"end":34.85,"words":[[29.73,29.86],[29.86,30.16],[30.16,30.28],[30.28,31.67],[31.89,32.43],[32.43,32.98],[32.98,33.28],[33.28,33.4],[33.4,34.43]]},{"el":"s0","text":"From 2008 to 2014 the Secure Communities program checked the fingerprints of everyone booked into local jails against immigration databases; a 2014 study found it did not measurably reduce crime.","start":35.2,"end":48.83,"words":[[35.24,35.52],[35.52,36.37],[36.37,36.51],[36.51,37.29],[37.29,37.43],[37.43,37.86],[37.86,38.56],[38.56,39.13],[39.13,39.48],[39.48,39.62],[39.62,40.4],[40.4,40.54],[40.54,41.04],[41.04,41.32],[41.32,41.6],[41.6,42.03],[42.03,42.45],[42.45,42.88],[42.88,43.58],[43.58,44.43],[44.68,44.82],[44.82,45.6],[45.6,45.95],[45.95,46.31],[46.31,46.45],[46.45,46.66],[46.66,46.87],[46.87,47.51],[47.51,47.93],[47.93,48.36]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Racial profiling","start":49.73,"end":51.33,"words":[[49.78,50.32],[50.32,51.21]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In Melendres v. Arpaio (2013), a federal court found that Maricopa County, Arizona, deputies under Sheriff Joe Arpaio had racially profiled Latino drivers during immigration sweeps.","start":52.03,"end":66.0,"words":[[52.08,52.24],[52.24,52.85],[52.85,53.08],[53.46,53.92],[53.92,54.84],[55.11,55.26],[55.26,55.8],[55.8,56.03],[56.03,56.41],[56.41,56.64],[56.64,57.33],[57.33,57.87],[58.13,58.82],[59.09,59.7],[59.7,60.01],[60.01,60.39],[60.39,60.7],[60.7,61.16],[61.16,61.39],[61.39,61.93],[61.93,62.61],[62.61,63.15],[63.15,63.69],[63.69,64.22],[64.22,64.99],[64.99,65.45]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Arpaio was later convicted of contempt for defying the court's orders, and was pardoned in 2017.","start":66.35,"end":72.97,"words":[[66.4,66.83],[66.83,67.05],[67.05,67.4],[67.4,68.05],[68.05,68.19],[68.19,68.77],[68.77,68.91],[68.91,69.41],[69.41,69.56],[69.56,69.84],[69.84,70.2],[70.45,70.67],[70.67,70.89],[70.89,71.32],[71.32,71.46],[71.46,72.54]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In September 2025 the Supreme Court allowed immigration stops in the Los Angeles area to resume while a challenge to their reliance on factors including apparent ethnicity continues (see “Borders”).","start":73.32,"end":86.3,"words":[[73.37,73.52],[73.52,74.14],[74.14,75.37],[75.37,75.53],[75.53,75.99],[75.99,76.22],[76.22,76.61],[76.61,77.38],[77.38,77.76],[77.76,77.92],[77.92,78.07],[78.07,78.3],[78.3,78.92],[78.92,79.3],[79.3,79.46],[79.46,79.92],[79.92,80.23],[80.23,80.38],[80.38,81.0],[81.0,81.15],[81.15,81.39],[81.39,82.0],[82.0,82.16],[82.16,82.62],[82.62,83.24],[83.24,83.78],[83.78,84.39],[84.39,85.09],[85.09,85.24],[85.24,85.7]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Detention","start":87.2,"end":88.14,"words":[[87.25,88.04]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Immigration detention reached record numbers in 2025.","start":88.84,"end":92.89,"words":[[88.89,89.55],[89.55,90.09],[90.09,90.42],[90.42,90.75],[90.75,91.15],[91.15,91.28],[91.28,92.42]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Detention centers are often run by private companies or county jails under contract.","start":93.24,"end":98.13,"words":[[93.29,93.82],[93.82,94.23],[94.23,94.29],[94.29,94.56],[94.56,94.76],[94.76,94.96],[94.96,95.43],[95.43,95.97],[95.97,96.03],[96.03,96.43],[96.43,96.83],[96.83,97.1],[97.1,97.7]]},{"el":"s2","text":"News investigations in 2025 found that U.S. citizens were among the people stopped and detained by immigration agents.","start":98.48,"end":106.63,"words":[[98.54,98.81],[98.81,99.76],[99.76,99.9],[99.9,100.98],[100.98,101.32],[101.32,101.53],[101.53,101.87],[102.21,102.75],[102.75,102.89],[102.89,103.16],[103.16,103.29],[103.29,103.63],[103.63,103.97],[103.97,104.18],[104.18,104.65],[104.65,104.86],[104.86,105.54],[105.54,106.15]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Do sanctuary policies affect crime?","start":107.53,"end":109.94,"words":[[107.58,107.71],[107.71,108.35],[108.35,108.8],[108.8,109.12],[109.12,109.5]]},{"el":"s3","text":"“Sanctuary” policies limit how much local police help with federal immigration enforcement, for example by declining to hold people on ICE detainer requests without a judicial warrant.","start":110.64,"end":122.02,"words":[[110.68,111.38],[111.38,111.87],[111.87,112.22],[112.22,112.43],[112.43,112.71],[112.71,113.13],[113.13,113.47],[113.47,113.75],[113.75,113.96],[113.96,114.45],[114.45,115.15],[115.15,115.85],[116.09,116.23],[116.23,116.79],[116.79,117.0],[117.0,117.63],[117.63,117.77],[117.77,118.12],[118.12,118.47],[118.47,118.61],[118.61,118.82],[118.82,119.3],[119.3,119.86],[119.86,120.28],[120.28,120.42],[120.42,120.98],[120.98,121.47]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Supporters say they keep immigrants willing to report crimes and serve as witnesses; opponents say they release people who should be deported.","start":122.37,"end":130.88,"words":[[122.41,122.95],[122.95,123.18],[123.18,123.41],[123.41,123.64],[123.64,124.34],[124.34,124.72],[124.72,124.88],[124.88,125.26],[125.26,125.72],[125.72,125.96],[125.96,126.19],[126.19,126.34],[126.34,127.03],[127.3,128.0],[128.0,128.23],[128.23,128.46],[128.46,128.84],[128.84,129.23],[129.23,129.38],[129.38,129.62],[129.62,129.77],[129.77,130.39]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Most studies find no increase in crime from sanctuary policies, but the debate continues and federal and state laws on the question keep changing.","start":131.23,"end":140.36,"words":[[131.28,131.63],[131.63,132.05],[132.05,132.4],[132.4,132.61],[132.61,133.03],[133.03,133.17],[133.17,133.51],[133.51,133.79],[133.79,134.49],[134.49,135.05],[135.29,135.5],[135.5,135.64],[135.64,136.06],[136.06,136.69],[136.69,136.9],[136.9,137.39],[137.39,137.6],[137.6,137.95],[137.95,138.16],[138.16,138.3],[138.3,138.44],[138.44,138.99],[138.99,139.2],[139.2,139.9]]},{"el":"h4","text":"What families can do","start":141.26,"end":142.85,"words":[[141.3,141.58],[141.58,142.25],[142.25,142.53],[142.53,142.72]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Know your rights at home and on the street (see “Your rights with police”).","start":143.55,"end":146.98,"words":[[143.6,143.79],[143.79,143.92],[143.92,144.24],[144.24,144.36],[144.36,144.62],[144.62,144.81],[144.81,144.94],[144.94,145.07],[145.07,145.39],[145.39,145.52],[145.52,145.64],[145.64,145.96],[145.96,146.16],[146.16,146.54]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Make a family preparedness plan: who picks up the children, where documents are, and a lawyer's number memorized.","start":147.33,"end":154.06,"words":[[147.38,147.64],[147.64,147.77],[147.77,148.16],[148.16,148.8],[148.8,149.13],[149.35,149.48],[149.48,149.74],[149.74,149.87],[149.87,150.0],[150.0,150.58],[150.81,151.0],[151.0,151.65],[151.65,151.77],[152.0,152.19],[152.19,152.32],[152.32,152.65],[152.65,152.97],[152.97,153.62]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Carry a “red card” stating your rights.","start":154.41,"end":157.05,"words":[[154.43,154.74],[154.74,154.9],[154.9,155.13],[155.13,155.37],[155.37,155.92],[155.92,156.08],[156.08,156.55]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Connect with local rapid-response networks and legal services.","start":157.4,"end":161.95,"words":[[157.42,157.89],[157.89,158.13],[158.13,158.6],[158.6,159.55],[159.55,160.1],[160.1,160.34],[160.34,160.73],[160.73,161.36]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Report false reports to police or immigration authorities that target people because of their ethnicity; that is exactly what CAREN-style laws address.","start":162.3,"end":171.67,"words":[[162.35,162.75],[162.75,163.06],[163.06,163.53],[163.53,163.69],[163.69,164.08],[164.08,164.16],[164.16,164.95],[164.95,165.58],[165.58,165.82],[165.82,166.21],[166.21,166.6],[166.6,167.0],[167.0,167.15],[167.15,167.39],[167.39,168.1],[168.37,168.61],[168.61,168.77],[168.77,169.4],[169.4,169.63],[169.63,170.42],[170.42,170.66],[170.66,171.13]]}]}